<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's bonos surged about one full point on Friday, heartened by below-forecast August consumer price growth, dealers said.</p>
<p>Inflation was 0.3 percent month on month, against forecasts of an average 0.5 percent rise.</p>
<p>Bonds should consolidate and may even capitalise on the gains next week, economists said.</p>
<p>A second wave of buying this afternoon was spurred by benign August U.S. retail sales and inflation data, allaying fears of an imminent hike in U.S. rates and boosting Treasuries.</p>
<p>The 10-yr September bond future hit a high of 103.52.</p>
</text>
